A||N||7||Monkeyman||Stereo in the trunk questions||||1||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-26-2001||08:25 PM||||I've just had a brain storm regarding my trunk.  I removed the carpet to shampoo it and realized how nice and square most of the corners are.  Here's my idea (which probably won't work).  Make the bottom of the trunk (the smaller area) into a ported bandpass sub box (no idea how I'd run the port--that's up to you guys to figure out for me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and use the upper (larger) section as an amp rack.  Here are the problems as I see them.  I'll get electronic noise through the RCA cables.  How can I shield them?  I'm limited as to the length of a port tube.  Any way of fooling the sub into thinking the tube is shorter?  Heat shouldn't be a concern as it would be easy enough to run a small tube to the outside (possibly with a small fan if necessary).<P>What's wrong with my thinking?  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MR2KLR||11-26-2001||10:22 PM||||Mounting the amps there is a good idea. putting subs there won't realy work. The engine noize/ resonance (SP) will kill most all of the bass.<P>A local shop near me (DR. AUDIO) did this in a 86/87 GT back about 1995 or so they moved the ECM up to the stock sub location and ran two 3" oval Fiberglass / Alu. ports around each side of the motor and out through the center console. they put four 12" subs in the trunk they also packed in two huge amps and another battery they finished of thier SPL beast with a "Good" set of 4X10's & 4X6's a CD player & 1/2 DIN EQ. all said and done they regret the fact that they did it. they say they put 1,000 of hours into the port work and box. they told me this after I asked them the same question you just asked the forum. they said NO it was a bad idea. and if anything like that would be done to do it from the front like <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  does.<P>PS. the SPL Fiero hit mid -to- high 140db in IASCA, USAC and IDBL comp. not very good at all, since a SINGLE Orion HCCA 12" and a HCCA 275R amp can hit over 140db up front at 1/10th the cost.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-27-2001||04:09 AM||||I've been trying to build a ported box up front, but I'm having difficulty getting some exact dimensions for a box.  I'm about ready to give up.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MR2KLR||11-27-2001||08:06 AM||||try makeing the box to fit the car as best as posible THEN fid out what size the box it and then pick a sub. good old <P>"Reverse enginering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> works for me"<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
